sis. Officer should inspect or refer.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 2, "calls": 2, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1225, "completion_tokens": 73}}, "cost_usd": 0.000106}}
{"task": "10 region outside corpus", "q": "When should I plant soybean in Kumasi?", "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["no local reference for region 'kumasi' (deciduous forest zone; corpus covers Northern Ghana only for this question)", "sources differ on planting window: APNI-SARI-2023, IITA-SSPING-2022", "sources differ on planting depth: APNI-SARI-2023, IITA-SSPING-2022", "sources differ on plant spacing: APNI-SARI-2023, IITA-SSPING-2022"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth", "RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:kumasi:2026-10-25"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023", true], ["IITA-SSPING-2022", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": true, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'The officer should decide based on the rainfall record for Kumasi from 2026-09-25 to 2026…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No guidance given"], "figures_checked": 21, "sentences_checked": 8, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "For soybean planting in Kumasi, choose a planting window.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages give window", "sent_to_judge": "For soybean planting in the farmer's area, choose a planting window."}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Do not plant too early before the rains are well established to avoid prolonged dry spells that may cause the plants to die [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture].", "cited": ["IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Choose a planting depth.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages give depth"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "Choose a plant spacing.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages give spacing"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "The officer should decide based on the rainfall record for Kumasi from 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-24, which shows 25 of 30 days with at least 1 mm of rain and a total of 158.8 mm [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:kumasi:2026-10-25].", "cited": ["RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:kumasi:2026-10-25"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No guidance given"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": true, "problems": [], "figures_checked": 21, "sentences_checked": 8, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "The planting window for soybean in the northern region is between mid-June and late July [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "However, another source suggests planting between mid-June to mid-July [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window].", "cited": ["IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Do not plant too early before the rains are well established to avoid prolonged dry spells that may cause the plants to die [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture].", "cited": ["IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "The rainfall record for Kumasi from 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-24 shows 25 of 30 days with at least 1 mm; total 158.8 mm [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:kumasi:2026-10-25].", "cited": ["RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:kumasi:2026-10-25"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "The officer should decide based on this record.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing", "RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:kumasi:2026-10-25"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage says so"}]}}]}, "draft": "Caution: the curated sources cover Northern Ghana only. The guidance below comes from them and may not apply in Kumasi; the officer should confirm local timing.\n\nThe planting window for soybean in the northern region is between mid-June and late July [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window]. However, another source suggests planting between mid-June to mid-July [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window]. The officer should choose. Do not plant too early before the rains are well established to avoid prolonged dry spells that may cause the plants to die [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture].\n\nFor planting depth, one source recommends making holes about 5 cm deep [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth], while another suggests a depth of 3 cm, not deeper than 5 cm [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth]. The officer should choose.\n\nFor plant spacing, one source recommends a row-to-row spacing of 50 cm and 15 cm between plants in a row [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing], while another suggests 50 cm between rows and 10 cm between plants within the rows [IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing]. The officer should choose.\n\nThe rainfall record for Kumasi from 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-24 shows 25 of 30 days with at least 1 mm; total 158.8 mm [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:kumasi:2026-10-25]. The officer should decide based on this record.\n\nNote: (officer only) Question received 25 Oct 2026. Windows cited: CSIR-SARI/APNI, northern region: between mid-June and late July; IITA, northern region: between mid-June to mid-July. The date is outside the cited windows.\nNote: (officer only) District Kumasi taken from the question text.\nNote: (officer only) Rainfall record [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:kumasi:2026-10-25] for Kumasi, 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-24: 25 rain days (at least 1 mm), 158.8 mm in total, 0 days missing (Open-Meteo (model-based estimate, forecast API past days)). This is a model estimate for one point in the district, not a rain gauge reading; estimates can differ a lot from a local gauge and from other providers. The guides give no rainfall amount that marks onset; AgriReach does not say whether onset has been reached. The officer decides.", "drafted_by": "model", "usage": {"attempted": 6, "calls": 6, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 3162, "completion_tokens": 686}, "judge": {"calls": 3, "prompt_tokens": 4431, "completion_tokens": 319}, "farmer_text": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 556, "completion_tokens": 159}}, "cost_usd": 0.001252}}
{"task": "11 Wa (Upper West) town name", "q": "When should I plant soybean at Wa?", "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["sources differ on planting window: APNI-SARI-2023, IITA-SSPING-2022", "sources differ on planting depth: APNI-SARI-2023, IITA-SSPING-2022", "sources differ on plant spacing: APNI-SARI-2023, IITA-SSPING-2022"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window", "APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth", "RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:wa:2026-10-25"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023", true], ["IITA-SSPING-2022", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": true, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": true, "problems": [], "figures_checked": 11, "sentences_checked": 5, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "- Planting Window: Choose between mid-June and late July [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window], or between mid-June and mid-July [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages match"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "- Planting Depth: Make planting holes about 5 cm deep [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth], or avoid deeper sowing (recommended depth = 3 cm; not deeper than 5 cm) [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages match"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "- Plant Spacing: Use a row-to-row spacing of 50 cm and 15 cm spacing between plants in a row [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing], or 50 cm between rows and 10 cm between plants within the rows [IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing", "IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages match"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "- Plant after the rains are well established to avoid prolonged dry spells [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture].", "cited": ["IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}]}}]}, "draft": "To plant soybean at Wa, consider the following guidelines:\n\n- Planting Window: Choose between mid-June and late July [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-planting-window], or between mid-June and mid-July [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-planting-window]. The officer should decide which to follow.\n- Planting Depth: Make planting holes about 5 cm deep [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-depth], or avoid deeper sowing (recommended depth = 3 cm; not deeper than 5 cm) [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-depth]. The officer should decide which to follow.\n- Plant Spacing: Use a row-to-row spacing of 50 cm and 15 cm spacing between plants in a row [APNI-SARI-2023:p11-spacing], or 50 cm between rows and 10 cm between plants within the rows [IITA-SSPING-2022:p17-spacing]. The officer should decide which to follow.\n- Plant after the rains are well established to avoid prolonged dry spells [IITA-SSPING-2022:p18-moisture].\n\nA rainfall record is attached for the officer's reference [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:wa:2026-10-25].\n\nNote: (officer only) Question received 25 Oct 2026. Windows cited: CSIR-SARI/APNI, northern region: between mid-June and late July; IITA, northern region: between mid-June to mid-July. The date is outside the cited windows.\nNote: (officer only) District Wa taken from the question text.\nNote: (officer only) Rainfall record [RAINFALL-OPEN-METEO:wa:2026-10-25] for Wa, 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-24: 17 rain days (at least 1 mm), 149.9 mm in total, 0 days missing (Open-Meteo (model-based estimate, forecast API past days)). This is a model estimate for one point in the district, not a rain gauge reading; estimates can differ a lot from a local gauge and from other providers. The guides give no rainfall amount that marks onset; AgriReach does not say whether onset has been reached. The officer decides.", "drafted_by": "model", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 1511, "completion_tokens": 307}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 3006, "completion_tokens": 183}, "farmer_text": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 472, "completion_tokens": 90}}, "cost_usd": 0.000907}}
